Subject: Move the operand-shuffle handlers out of the interpreter's dispatch body

What this does
  Gives the eight operand-shuffle opcodes out-of-line handler functions and
  leaves a call in each interpreter case.

Why we need it
  Each inline case declared a temporary JSValue and performed the shuffle inside
  JS_CallInternal. Every such local enlarges that function's stack frame and
  every such body adds to its code, and both are paid on every interpreted call,
  whether or not the shuffle executes. The frames multiply with interpreter
  recursion depth.

What it adds
  Eight noinline helpers -- perm3, rot3l, rot4l, rot5l, rot3r, perm4, perm5 and
  swap2 -- whose bodies are the shuffles the cases performed, each replaced by a
  single call. The opcodes, their stack effects and the values moved are
  unchanged. No opcode is added or retired and BC_VERSION is unchanged.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
